    "summary": "pypi-publish action revocation of CA in the chain that Sigstore uses in Trusted Publishing and Digital Attestations for PyPI",
    "description": "### Summary\n\nThe [pypi-publish action][pypi-publish] versions before 1.14.2 used to bundle the `emSign` root CA trust store certificate through the `certifi` distribution. It has since been removed through the bundle and the new version no longer includes them.\n\n[pypi-publish]: https://github.com/marketplace/actions/pypi-publish\n\n### Details\n\nThe `certifi`-provided TLS trust store is typically used by many projects in the Python ecosystem, including Sigstore that [pypi-publish] relies on for Trusted Publishing and Digital Attestations.\n\n### Related\n\nThe external compromise is being tracked at https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com",
