    "ghsa_id": "GHSA-m4w4-3r8h-jw98",
    "cve_id": "CVE-2026-35002",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-m4w4-3r8h-jw98",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-m4w4-3r8h-jw98",
    "summary": "Agno: Arbitrary code execution via `eval()` on `field_type` in `FunctionCall`",
    "description": "### Impact\nAgno versions prior to 2.3.24 contain an arbitrary code execution vulnerability\nin the model execution component. The `field_type` parameter on a `FunctionCall`\ninput field was passed to Python's built-in `eval()`, allowing an attacker who\ncould influence that value to execute arbitrary Python code in the Agno process.\n\nThis is a code injection flaw (CWE-95) with full impact to confidentiality,\nintegrity, and availability. CVSS 3.1 score: 9.3 (Critical).\n\nAny deployment that exposes Agno to user-influenced FunctionCall inputs\n(for example via an API, web UI, or untrusted tool/model output) is affected.\n\n### Patches\nFixed in **Agno 2.3.24**.\n\nThe unsafe `eval()` call was replaced with a fixed `type_mapping` dictionary\nlookup, and `field_type` is now validated as either a known string key or an\nalready-resolved `type` object before use. See commit\n[cbf67552](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/commit/cbf675521d4d2281925a051784a3b94172e56416)\n(PR #5912).\n\nAll users should upgrade to 2.3.24 or later. The current release line (2.6.x)\nincludes the fix.\n\n### Workarounds\nThere is no safe workaround. Users who cannot upgrade should ensure no\nuntrusted input can reach the `field_type` parameter of `FunctionCall`\ninput fields, but upgrading is strongly preferred.\n\n### References\n- Patch commit: https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/commit/cbf675521d4d2281925a051784a3b94172e56416\n- Patch PR: https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/pull/5912\n- CWE-95: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/95.html",
