    "summary": "obsidian-tc tokens can access arbitrary configured vaults",
    "description": "### Impact\nTool dispatch did not check the caller-supplied `input.vault` against the caller's bound vault (`ctx.vaultId`); the folder ACL was a single global instance and the JWT carried no vault claim. As a result, **any valid token could read, write, or delete any configured vault** by passing `input.vault`, defeating multi-tenant isolation across ~90 tool sites. (`resources/read` was the only surface that already guarded this.)\n\n### Patches\nFixed in **1.3.1** (the fix was developed on the `v1.3.0` tag, which never published to npm; 1.3.1 is the first published release with the fix). Upgrade to `>= 1.3.1`.\n\n### Workarounds\nRun a single vault per server process, or isolate each tenant on a separate process/credential.\n\n### Fix\nA central `input.vault === ctx.vaultId` guard was added in dispatch before the scope check.",
